<title>USA: Microdyne sees expenses affecting 1997.</title>
<headline>Microdyne sees expenses affecting 1997.</headline>
<dateline>ALEXANDRIA, Va. 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Microdyne Corp, reporting lower fiscal fourth quarter and full-year results, said Thursday that non-operating expenses would affect earnings in 1997.</p>
<p>The company said its $2.1 million of interest expense in 1996 was equivalent to $0.10 per share on a fully taxed basis.</p>
<p>It said it expects to generate more than $5 million in cash per quarter, which it expects to use to repay bank debt.</p>
<p>Unless it diverts funds to acquisitions or other uses, the company believes it has the ability to erase its bank debt before the end of 1997, it said.</p>
</text>
